{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoRootLabelling","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoRootLabelling","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoRootStructure","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.ImplicitScalar","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Calculus.Deriv.MeanValue","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Trigonometric.Deriv","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Sqrt"],"declarations":68,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.hasDerivAt_Ypair_snd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.hasDerivAt_Ypair_snd","kind":"theorem","line":742,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoRootLabelling.lean#L742-L760","doc":"**`Y₃`, the conjugate branch.** Same hypothesis, opposite sign on the\nimaginary part. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.curve_Ypair","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.curve_Ypair","kind":"theorem","line":716,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoRootLabelling.lean#L716-L740","doc":"**`Y₂` and `Y₃` are roots of the curve.**\n\n`unitCubic c Y = (Y − t)(Y² + βY + γ)` with `β = t − 2c`, `γ = t² − 2ct + 2c + 1`\n— an identity whose constant term needs `gamma_rel`, `t·γ = 1`. So a root of the\ncofactor is a root of the cubic, hence of the curve. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.pair_quadratic_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.pair_quadratic_zero","kind":"theorem","line":706,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoRootLabelling.lean#L706-L714","doc":"**The quadratic cofactor vanishes at both members of the pair** — Vieta,\nvia `otherRoots_factor`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.curve_Yreal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.curve_Yreal","kind":"theorem","line":689,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoRootLabelling.lean#L689-L704","doc":"**`Y₁` is a root of the curve.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.im_div_Ypair_snd_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.im_div_Ypair_snd_pos","kind":"theorem","line":672,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoRootLabelling.lean#L672-L679","doc":"**`logSumB`'s second sign fact**, likewise. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.im_div_Ypair_fst_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.im_div_Ypair_fst_pos","kind":"theorem","line":665,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoRootLabelling.lean#L665-L670","doc":"**`logSumB`'s first sign fact**, from `logSumA`'s second via conjugation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.im_mul_Ypair_fst_neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.im_mul_Ypair_fst_neg","kind":"theorem","line":659,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoRootLabelling.lean#L659-L663","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.im_mul_Ypair_snd_neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.im_mul_Ypair_snd_neg","kind":"theorem","line":654,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoRootLabelling.lean#L654-L657","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.im_div_eq_neg_im_mul_conj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.im_div_eq_neg_im_mul_conj","kind":"theorem","line":647,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoRootLabelling.lean#L647-L652","doc":"`Im(y/x) = −Im(x·conj y)` on the unit circle. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.Ypair_conj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.Ypair_conj","kind":"theorem","line":640,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoRootLabelling.lean#L640-L645","doc":"The pair are complex conjugates off the collision. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.one_sub_Ypair_mem_slitPlane","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.one_sub_Ypair_mem_slitPlane","kind":"theorem","line":617,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoRootLabelling.lean#L617-L622","doc":"**`1 − y` is off `log`'s cut at the pair**, which is `|arg(1−y)| < π/2` — the\nfirst of G13's two tight groupings, and the one that is elementary. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.re_Ypair_lt_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.re_Ypair_lt_one","kind":"theorem","line":609,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoRootLabelling.lean#L609-L615","doc":"**`Re y < 1` at the pair.** `cos φ ≤ 1` and `t > 0`; nothing else is needed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.re_Ypair_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.re_Ypair_eq","kind":"theorem","line":601,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoRootLabelling.lean#L601-L607","doc":"At the pair, `Re y = cos φ − t/2` — both members share it, being conjugates. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.vieta_hv2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.vieta_hv2","kind":"theorem","line":572,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoRootLabelling.lean#L572-L578","doc":"**`hv₂`.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.vieta_hv1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.vieta_hv1","kind":"theorem","line":564,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoRootLabelling.lean#L564-L570","doc":"**`hv₁` in the form `logSumA_eq_log` wants it.** Both this and `hv₂` collapse\nto `unitCircle_quadratic`; the labelling contributes only `e₁ = 2c`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.vieta_e3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.vieta_e3","kind":"theorem","line":551,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoRootLabelling.lean#L551-L562","doc":"`e₃ = t·y₂·y₃ = 1` — this is `gamma_rel`, and it is the one with content. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.vieta_e2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.vieta_e2","kind":"theorem","line":540,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoRootLabelling.lean#L540-L549","doc":"`e₂ = t·y₂ + t·y₃ + y₂y₃ = 2c + 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.vieta_e1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.vieta_e1","kind":"theorem","line":531,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoRootLabelling.lean#L531-L538","doc":"`e₁ = t + y₂ + y₃ = 2c`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.Ypair_prod","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.Ypair_prod","kind":"theorem","line":528,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoRootLabelling.lean#L528-L529","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.Ypair_sum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.Ypair_sum","kind":"theorem","line":525,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoRootLabelling.lean#L525-L526","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.hasDerivAt_Ypair_snd_real","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.hasDerivAt_Ypair_snd_real","kind":"theorem","line":499,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoRootLabelling.lean#L499-L515","doc":"**`Y₃` on the real branch.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.hasDerivAt_Ypair_fst_real","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.hasDerivAt_Ypair_fst_real","kind":"theorem","line":481,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoRootLabelling.lean#L481-L497","doc":"**`Y₂` on the real branch.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.Ypair_of_disc_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.Ypair_of_disc_pos","kind":"theorem","line":472,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoRootLabelling.lean#L472-L479","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.hasDerivAt_pairDisc","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.hasDerivAt_pairDisc","kind":"theorem","line":465,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoRootLabelling.lean#L465-L470","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.eventually_disc_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.eventually_disc_pos","kind":"theorem","line":461,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoRootLabelling.lean#L461-L463","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.hasDerivAt_Ypair_fst","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.hasDerivAt_Ypair_fst","kind":"theorem","line":424,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoRootLabelling.lean#L424-L446","doc":"**`Y₂` is differentiable wherever the pair has not collided.**\n\nThe hypothesis `pairDisc φ < 0` is doing two separate jobs, and both are needed:\nit selects `otherRoots`' complex branch, and it keeps `√` away from `0`. At `φ₀`\nboth fail at once — which is exactly why `φ₀` is the exceptional point\n`envelopeS_total` is built to tolerate, rather than an artefact of this proof. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.pairNegDisc_eq_neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.pairNegDisc_eq_neg","kind":"theorem","line":421,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoRootLabelling.lean#L421-L422","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.eventually_disc_neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.eventually_disc_neg","kind":"theorem","line":415,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoRootLabelling.lean#L415-L419","doc":"`pairDisc < 0` on a whole neighbourhood — needed because `HasDerivAt` is a\nstatement about the function *near* `φ`, not at it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.Ypair_of_disc_neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.Ypair_of_disc_neg","kind":"theorem","line":403,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoRootLabelling.lean#L403-L413","doc":"**The complex branch, identified.** `pairDisc φ < 0` selects `otherRoots`'\nsecond case. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.hasDerivAt_pairIm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.hasDerivAt_pairIm","kind":"theorem","line":396,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoRootLabelling.lean#L396-L401","doc":"Differentiable exactly where the pair has not collided — `√` is the only\nthing in the way, and `pairNegDisc φ > 0` is what clears it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.pairIm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.pairIm","kind":"def","line":393,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoRootLabelling.lean#L393-L394","doc":"The imaginary half-width of the complex pair. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.hasDerivAt_pairNegDisc","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.hasDerivAt_pairNegDisc","kind":"theorem","line":386,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoRootLabelling.lean#L386-L391","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.pairNegDisc'","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.pairNegDisc'","kind":"def","line":379,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoRootLabelling.lean#L379-L384","doc":"`d/dφ` of the above, named to keep the statements readable. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.pairNegDisc","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.pairNegDisc","kind":"def","line":376,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoRootLabelling.lean#L376-L377","doc":"`4γ − β²`, positive exactly where the pair is genuinely complex. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.continuous_Ypair","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.continuous_Ypair","kind":"theorem","line":348,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoRootLabelling.lean#L348-L363","doc":"**The pair is continuous on the whole arc, collision included.**\n\n`continuous_otherRoots` is continuous *through* the branch collision — at\n`β² = 4γ` both of its branches give `(−β/2, −β/2)` — and the coefficients are\ncontinuous because `realRootPath` is. So `envelopeS`'s continuity hypothesis on\n`Icc 0 π` is available with no exceptional point; only the *derivative* needs one,\nand `envelopeS_total` is built to tolerate exactly that asymmetry. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.Ypair","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.Ypair","kind":"def","line":345,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoRootLabelling.lean#L345-L346","doc":"The colliding pair, as a function of `φ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.continuous_pairDisc","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.continuous_pairDisc","kind":"theorem","line":342,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoRootLabelling.lean#L342-L343","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.continuous_pairGamma","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.continuous_pairGamma","kind":"theorem","line":339,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoRootLabelling.lean#L339-L340","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.continuous_pairBeta","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.continuous_pairBeta","kind":"theorem","line":336,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoRootLabelling.lean#L336-L337","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.pairDisc","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.pairDisc","kind":"def","line":332,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoRootLabelling.lean#L332-L334","doc":"The pair's discriminant along the arc. Its sign flips exactly at the\ncollision `φ₀` (Route 36 G5), so both branches of `otherRoots` are live. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.hasDerivAt_pairGamma","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.hasDerivAt_pairGamma","kind":"theorem","line":320,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoRootLabelling.lean#L320-L330","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.hasDerivAt_pairBeta","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.hasDerivAt_pairBeta","kind":"theorem","line":312,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoRootLabelling.lean#L312-L318","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.pairGamma","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.pairGamma","kind":"def","line":309,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoRootLabelling.lean#L309-L310","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.pairBeta","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.pairBeta","kind":"def","line":306,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoRootLabelling.lean#L306-L307","doc":"The quadratic cofactor's coefficients along the arc: `Y² + βY + γ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.hasDerivAt_realRootPath'","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.hasDerivAt_realRootPath'","kind":"theorem","line":303,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoRootLabelling.lean#L303-L304","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.realRootPath'","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.realRootPath'","kind":"def","line":297,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoRootLabelling.lean#L297-L301","doc":"`d/dφ realRootPath` — named so the statements below stay readable. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.continuous_realRootPath","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.continuous_realRootPath","kind":"theorem","line":286,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoRootLabelling.lean#L286-L287","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.unitCubic_realRootPath","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.unitCubic_realRootPath","kind":"theorem","line":281,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoRootLabelling.lean#L281-L284","doc":"`Yreal` solves the cubic — the reason it is a *root* path and not just a\nsmooth curve. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.Yreal_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.Yreal_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":276,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoRootLabelling.lean#L276-L279","doc":"`Yreal` never vanishes — it is a root in `(0,1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.hasDerivAt_Yreal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.hasDerivAt_Yreal","kind":"theorem","line":269,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoRootLabelling.lean#L269-L274","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.Yreal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.Yreal","kind":"def","line":259,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoRootLabelling.lean#L259-L267","doc":"**`Y₁`, the labelling's real branch.**\n\nWritten as `((· : ℝ) : ℂ)` of a *real* function on purpose, not as a `ℂ`-valued\nfunction that happens to take real values. `hasDerivAt_log_neg_ofReal` — route 2\nof `log_neg_route`, the only route available at the positive real root — is\nstated for exactly this shape, and no pointwise fact about roots can supply it.\nRoute 36 G8/G9: the positive real root is where route 1 is *impossible*, and this\nis the root that carries it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.hasDerivAt_realRootPath","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.hasDerivAt_realRootPath","kind":"theorem","line":245,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoRootLabelling.lean#L245-L257","doc":"**`realRootPath` is differentiable at every `φ`** — no exceptional point.\n\n`cos φ ≤ 1 < 3/2` unconditionally, so `hasDerivAt_realRoot` applies everywhere on\nthe arc and the chain rule does the rest. This is where the widened bound of §1b\npays: with `c < 1` this statement would have had to exclude `φ = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.realRootPath_lt_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.realRootPath_lt_one","kind":"theorem","line":243,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoRootLabelling.lean#L243-L243","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.realRootPath_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.realRootPath_pos","kind":"theorem","line":241,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoRootLabelling.lean#L241-L241","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.realRootPath","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.realRootPath","kind":"def","line":238,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoRootLabelling.lean#L238-L239","doc":"The real root along the transport arc, as a function of `φ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.continuousAt_realRoot","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.continuousAt_realRoot","kind":"theorem","line":229,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoRootLabelling.lean#L229-L231","doc":"`realRoot` is continuous wherever it is differentiable. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.hasDerivAt_realRoot","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.hasDerivAt_realRoot","kind":"theorem","line":196,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoRootLabelling.lean#L196-L227","doc":"**`realRoot` is differentiable, with the implicit-function derivative.**\n\nd/dc realRoot c = −2·t·(1−t) / (3t² − 4ct + 2c + 1),    t = realRoot c\n\n`hc : c < 1` is strict on purpose — see the module docstring. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.hasStrictFDerivAt_unitCubic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.hasStrictFDerivAt_unitCubic","kind":"theorem","line":174,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoRootLabelling.lean#L174-L192","doc":"The strict derivative of `(c,t) ↦ unitCubic c t`, with partials\n`∂/∂c = −2t² + 2t` and `∂/∂t = 3t² − 4ct + 2c + 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.eq_realRoot'","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.eq_realRoot'","kind":"theorem","line":160,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoRootLabelling.lean#L160-L170","doc":"**Uniqueness on `c < 3/2`** — the two regimes combined.\n\n`c ≤ 1` goes through `real_root_neg_of_ne`; `1 < c < 3/2` goes through strict\nmonotonicity, which needs no root structure. The overlap is what lets `c = 1` be\nan interior point rather than an endpoint. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.strictMono_unitCubic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.strictMono_unitCubic","kind":"theorem","line":153,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoRootLabelling.lean#L153-L158","doc":"**`unitCubic c` is strictly increasing for `1/2 ≤ c ≤ 3/2`**, hence injective,\nhence has at most one real root anywhere. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.unitCubic_deriv_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.unitCubic_deriv_pos","kind":"theorem","line":143,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoRootLabelling.lean#L143-L151","doc":"**The `t`-derivative is positive for every `t`, when `1/2 ≤ c ≤ 3/2`.**\n\nNot the same statement as `unitCubic_deriv_ge`, which bounds it *at a root* in\n`(0,1)`. Here there is no root hypothesis and no constraint on `t` — which is\nwhat strict monotonicity needs. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.hasDerivAt_unitCubic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.hasDerivAt_unitCubic","kind":"theorem","line":129,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoRootLabelling.lean#L129-L141","doc":"`d/dt unitCubic c t = 3t² − 4ct + (2c+1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.eq_realRoot","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.eq_realRoot","kind":"theorem","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoRootLabelling.lean#L98-L114","doc":"**Uniqueness, and it is stronger than \"unique in `(0,1)`\".**\n\nEvery *positive* real root of `unitCubic c` equals `realRoot c` — no upper bound\nneeded, because `real_root_neg_of_ne` makes every root other than `realRoot c`\nnegative outright. The first draft carried `r < 1` and Lean flagged it as unused;\ndropping it is the honest statement.\n\nThat also lines up with Route 36 G8, which measures exactly **one** positive real\nroot at every arc point: this is that fact, in the form a proof can use. It is\nwhat makes `realRoot` a function rather than a choice, and what lets a local IFT\nsolution be identified with it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.unitCubic_realRoot","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.unitCubic_realRoot","kind":"theorem","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoRootLabelling.lean#L95-L96","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.realRoot_lt_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.realRoot_lt_one","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoRootLabelling.lean#L93-L93","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.realRoot_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.realRoot_pos","kind":"theorem","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoRootLabelling.lean#L91-L91","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.realRoot_mem_Ioo","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.realRoot_mem_Ioo","kind":"theorem","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoRootLabelling.lean#L88-L89","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.realRoot","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.realRoot","kind":"def","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoRootLabelling.lean#L85-L86","doc":"**The root of `unitCubic c` in `(0,1)`.** Single-valued by `eq_realRoot`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}